course: dictionary
lesson: 13896
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can name a thing, show an action, or give a sly sense of doing something, depending on the sentence. A ladle is a big, deep spoon with a long handle. «The cook filled the bowl with a ladle of hot soup.» Here ladle names a thing you hold.
explain: Ladle can also be a doing word. «Mum ladled the soup into six bowls.» Ladle is the action: she moved the soup from the pot into the bowls with a ladle. Ask yourself: is this word a thing, or is someone doing something?
explain: Look at the ending to spot the job. «She ladles soup every day» and «He ladled the soup yesterday» both use the verb. Ladles, ladled and ladling all come from the same root, so the word keeps its meaning.
explain: Context can stretch a word further. «The head teacher ladled out praise for the whole class.» Nobody is holding a spoon here. Ladle out means to give out a lot of something, so the class received a generous amount of praise.
fact: A ladle is a big, deep spoon with a long handle, used to serve soup or sauce.
fact: To ladle means to serve or move liquid with a ladle, as in «Sam ladled hot custard onto every plate.»
fact: Ladle out means to give out a lot of something, such as praise or advice.
fact: Ladle can be a noun (a ladle) or a verb (to ladle, ladles, ladled, ladling).
fact: In maths problems, a ladle can hold a set amount, such as 250 millilitres, so you can count how many ladles fill a jug.
exercise: «The cook used a big ladle to serve the soup.» What is a ladle in this sentence? | A kind of knife | *A big deep spoon with a long handle | A small fork for salad | A bowl with a lid
exercise: «Sam ladled hot custard onto every plate.» What does ladled mean? | To wash the dishes | *To serve liquid with a ladle | To cut into small squares | To freeze quickly
exercise: «The head teacher ladled out praise for the whole class.» What does ladle out mean here? | To spill by accident | To pour the water away | *To give out a lot of something | To hide in a cupboard
test: Each ladle holds 250 millilitres. How much soup do 4 ladles hold? | 750 millilitres | 500 millilitres | 1250 millilitres | *1000 millilitres
test: Which word is a verb in «Mum ladles soup at tea time»? | *ladles | time | tea | soup
exam: Which sentence uses ladle as a noun? | She ladled soup into the pot. | *The ladle hung above the stove. | He is ladling the broth now. | They ladled out treats all day.
